    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S2158\n\nSPONSOR: PALUMBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to the eligibility of enrolled members of Southampton\nVillage Ocean Rescue for the tax exemption on real property authorized\nby section 466-c of the real property tax law\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation recognizes the work and commitment of the Southampton\nVillage Ocean Rescue by granting eligibility for tax exemption on real\nproperty tax to enrolled members.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Introduces a tax exemption on real property (as authorized in\nsection 466-c of the real property tax law) for current members of\nSouthampton Village Ocean Rescue. It also clarifies the conditions what\nwould allow them to obtain such exemption.\n\nSection 2. Sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nFounded in April 2018, the Southampton Village Ocean Rescue (SVOR)\nresponds to emergencies in the ocean and bay, throughout the village of\nSouthampton. They are dedicated to making expeditious and safe water\nrescues year round at all unprotected beaches in Southampton village.\n\nEach month SVOR trains in different locations coordinating with numerous\nemergency agencies to be prepared for a multitude of aquatic emergen-\ncies. They work with the town and village lifeguard agencies as well as\nthe police and fire departments and consistently adapt to new protocols\nto ensure proper rescue techniques that best protect the victims and\nrescuers. SVOR rescuers are ocean lifeguard and CPR certified. They\npromote water safety and educate the public on the dangers of rip\ncurrents\n\nTo recognize these valuable services and bolster recruitment and\nretention efforts, this legislation sets forth criteria to authorize the\nvillage of Southampton to adopt a local law to make enrolled members of\nSVOR eligible for the same real property tax exemption enjoyed by their\nemergency responder counterparts in the volunteer fire and volunteer\nambulance services.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2022 S.8605/A.9626\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTBD\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the first of January next succeeding the\ndate which it shall have become a law and shall apply to taxable status\ndates occurring on or after such a date.\n",
